---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/analytics';
const title = "Measure cart recovery revenue without confusing attribution with lift";
const desc = "Build a decision record that distinguishes credited orders from additional profit. A clicked recovery email does not establish what the shopper would have done without it.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">{desc}</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-12">
      <h2>Define the unit before the dashboard</h2>
      <p>Specify whether enrollment is by customer, checkout or cart. Keep an event ledger with assignment time, eligibility reason, flow version, message attempts and order IDs. Deduplicate orders across email, SMS and platform reports; retain the original currency and a documented conversion rule.</p>
      <h2>Design a proposed comparison</h2>
      <p>Randomly assign eligible customers to recovery and holdout groups before messages are queued, keeping repeat visits in the same assignment. Define the observation window and primary outcome before launch. Log accidental messages to holdouts rather than silently deleting those customers. A before/after holiday comparison also includes seasonality and should not be described as causal lift.</p>
      <h2>Reconcile orders to economics</h2>
      <p>Start with order revenue before discounts and refunds. Subtract discounts and refunds once to obtain net revenue, then subtract product and variable fulfillment costs to obtain contribution. Compare both per eligible assigned customer, including customers who buy nothing, and assess total implementation cost. Report group sizes and uncertainty; a small positive difference is not proof of a profitable rollout.</p>
      <h2>Investigate disagreement</h2>
      <p>If the supplier dashboard exceeds the order ledger, check attribution windows, view-through credit, duplicate channels, canceled orders and taxes or shipping included in revenue. Save report settings with each export so a changed window cannot masquerade as improvement.</p>
      <h2>Evaluate analytics access</h2>
      <p>Ask candidate tools for exportable assignment, suppression and order records, not just a revenue tile. Sequenzy can remain on a shortlist if it can demonstrate the required event mapping and exports for your store; this page has not verified that integration. Reject a measurement design that cannot account for eligible non-buyers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
